      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By 1931, South Congress was finally paved all the way from the river to the railroad at present‑day Ben White Boulevard.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Congress",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The area's renaissance began at the intersection of South Congress and Monroe by putting historic buildings to good use to attract eclectic retail, arts, music venues and restaurants.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Congress",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Visitors can enjoy everything from gourmet tacos to artisan coffee while strolling past landmarks like the “Greetings from Austin” and “I love you so much” mural.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.southcongressavenue.com/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
